  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-LBN153</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced implementation of social protection strategy and reforms</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon continues to face the effects of compounded political, economic and social crises, further aggravated by intensified cross-border hostilities and broader regional instability. These developments have placed significant pressure on workers and their families, with heightened risks for persons with disabilities and other groups in vulnerable situations.
In line with the 2024 National Social Protection Strategy, the ILO supports tripartite constituents in strengthening a shock-responsive and financially sustainable social protection system that provides lifecycle income protection and can respond effectively during periods of crisis.

The intervention supports the Ministry of Social Affairs in establishing an inclusive governance structure to oversee implementation of the National Social Protection Strategy and guide the formulation, implementation and monitoring of social protection policies, programmes and schemes. It also supports the development of a Management Information System for the Rights and Access Programme, which provides the administrative foundation for the National Disability Allowance.
The ILO also provides technical support to the implementation of the new pension scheme under Law No. 319, which will replace the End-of-Service Indemnity for approximately 300,000 private sector workers. Through technical guidance, financial and actuarial analysis, support to social dialogue, and institutional capacity-building, the intervention contributes to improved governance of the National Social Security Fund and more adequate old-age income protection.
The expected result is a stronger, more inclusive and better-governed social protection system that benefits workers, persons with disabilities, older persons, families and groups in vulnerable situations, while strengthening the capacity of national institutions and social partners to design, finance and implement rights-based social protection measures.</narrative>
  </description>
